# Issue: genNumEqInsts decomposes the more structured side of NumEq#(t, t')
# and chose it with ordPair (Ord Type), i.e. by type variables' string-intern
# ids, an order bsc -u takes from how the root lists its imports; so
# Bug782_Div_OK was rejected with T0030 behind a scrambler package.
# Fix: both ordPair sites use ordPairBy cmpTypeShape, an order by content.
# Probe: compile the Classic translation alone, with -u behind a scrambler
# that interns its type variables in reverse order, and under
# -trace-intern-reverse; all compiles must succeed and dump the same .bo.

batching_bo_pair Bug782_Div_OK_Batch.bs Bug782_Div_OK_BatchTop.bs Bug782_Div_OK_BatchPre.bs
reverse_intern_same_bo Bug782_Div_OK_Batch.bs
